**Day 34: MongoDB Query Operators & Filters**  

**Topic:**  
Exploration of MongoDB query operators ($eq, $gt, $lt, $in, $and, $or, $not) and filtering techniques, including projection, sorting, limit, and skip. Practical application on a student collection.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand and apply comparison operators ($eq, $gt, $lt, $in).  
• Combine conditions using logical operators ($and, $or, $not).  
• Optimize queries with projection, sorting, and pagination (limit & skip).  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Wrote 12 queries using diverse operators on the student collection.  
• Practiced filtering, sorting, and limiting results in MongoDB Compass.  
• Analyzed query performance and output accuracy.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **Projection:** Selectively retrieves fields to reduce data transfer.  
• **Compound Queries:** Combine multiple conditions for precise filtering.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `db.students.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } })`  
• `db.students.find({ $or: [ { grade: "A" }, { attendance: { $gt: 90 } } ] })`  
• `db.students.find({}, { name: 1, grade: 1 }).sort({ grade: -1 }).limit(5)`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Filtering e-commerce products by price range ($gt, $lt).  
• Retrieving active users based on multiple criteria ($and, $or).  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• **MongoDB 7**  
• **Compass GUI**  

**Summary:**  
Mastered essential MongoDB query operators and filtering techniques, enabling efficient data retrieval and manipulation. Applied skills through hands-on queries and performance analysis.  

